==Candidates==
{{main article|Candidates of the Australian federal election, 2016}}
At the close of nominations on 9 June 2016, there were 1,625 candidates in total – 994 for the House of Representatives and 631 for the Senate. The number of Senate candidates was the highest ever at an Australian election, increased from 529 in 2013.<ref name="candidate-summary">{{cite news|last1=Green|first1=Antony|title=Summary of Candidates and Parties for the 2016 Federal election|url=http://blogs.abc.net.au/antonygreen/2016/06/close-of-nominations-2016-federal-election.html|accessdate=12 June 2016|date=10 June 2016}}</ref>

